# Agents the Ralph runners may use. Copy this file to `agents` (ignored by Git) and edit the copy.
#
# Format, one agent per line: stage|agent|model|effort|probe
#   stage   worker: `ralph`, `ralph-afk` and the `ralph-afk --pr` workers.
#           reviewer: the `ralph-afk --pr` reviewer only; sequential mode ignores these lines.
#   agent   A Ralph agent plugin, as listed by `ralph-tui plugins agents`. --pr uses claude and codex lines only.
#   model   Work model, passed as --model. RALPH_<AGENT>_MODEL overrides it for `ralph` and `ralph-afk`.
#   effort  Reasoning effort for --pr agents; - keeps the CLI default. `ralph` and `ralph-afk` ignore it.
#   probe   Cheap request run in /tmp. The agent is usable when the reply contains "pong".
#           Claude (with stream-json) and Codex probes also report when a usage limit resets.
#
# In --pr mode, line order within a stage is the fallback order.
# RALPH_AFK_SCHEDULE decides which agents may run in each hour; -a narrows that for one run.
# The commented-out lines are optional agents whose probes alone have been checked;
# choose a work model before enabling one.

worker|claude|sonnet|high|claude -p 'Reply with exactly: pong' --model haiku --effort low --output-format stream-json --verbose
worker|codex|gpt-6.2-sol|medium|codex exec --skip-git-repo-check --ephemeral -s read-only -m gpt-6-luna -c 'model_reasoning_effort="low"' 'Reply with exactly: pong'
reviewer|claude|opus|high|claude -p 'Reply with exactly: pong' --model haiku --effort low --output-format stream-json --verbose
#worker|cursor|auto|-|agent -p --trust --mode ask --model auto 'Reply with exactly: pong'
#worker|github-copilot|MODEL|-|copilot -s --no-custom-instructions --disable-builtin-mcps -p 'Reply with exactly: pong'
